NAME: EOD VA escalation
OWNER: Sales Manager
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every day at 12:30 PM
MILESTONE: 2
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Dan says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/spike-team/context/routines-on.md. If "EOD VA escalation" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", write "EOD VA escalation: not switched on" to this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/ and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Dan only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/spike-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/spike-team/context/owner.md is missing, write NO_CLIENT_SOURCE to the log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, write "no change" and stop.
Run record: end every run with one line in this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/: the time, "EOD VA escalation", and done, no change, not switched on, blocked (why) or failed (why), with counts. If you stopped at the switch check or the isolation guard, the line you wrote there is this run's record; don't add a second.

Re-read yesterday's EOD window. If you can't read the EOD channels or the roster, message nobody: write "EOD channels unreadable (<reason>)" to today's sales.md, record the run as blocked and stop. If nobody is missing, stop. If today's sales.md shows the VA was already messaged, don't message again. If /workspace/spike-team/context/eod-mode.md says "live", send the VA named in /workspace/spike-team/context/owner.md standing approval 4's exact text with the missing names, using the slack-api skill. In preview, write "would have messaged the VA: <names>" to today's sales.md instead. Add the names to today's note for the morning brief either way.
Before each team post, run the slack-api skill's sent check, so nothing is posted twice.
